<section class="page-lead page-shell" aria-labelledby="engineering-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">Field notes / 03 · Engineering</p>
  <h1 id="engineering-title">The boundary is part of the <em>architecture.</em></h1>
  <p class="lead-copy">A credible system tells a person what it owns, which action it can take, how its state survives, and what evidence supports its claims. Those questions appear differently in each ForgeWire Labs project.</p>
</section>

<section class="engineering-principles page-shell" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
  <div class="section-heading section-heading--stacked">
    <p class="eyebrow">Design questions</p>
    <h2 id="principles-title">What must stay legible?</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="principle-ledger">
    <article><span class="ledger-number">01</span><h3>Durable state</h3><p>Keep intent, decisions, project state, and observed results somewhere a later person or tool can inspect.</p></article>
    <article><span class="ledger-number">02</span><h3>Scoped authority</h3><p>Make it clear who owns a record and which actions a person, agent, provider, or interface is allowed to request.</p></article>
    <article><span class="ledger-number">03</span><h3>Visible failure</h3><p>Surface errors and unresolved limits. A successful operation is evidence for that run and environment; broader reliability depends on tested scope.</p></article>
    <article><span class="ledger-number">04</span><h3>Human intervention</h3><p>Keep review and decision points in the workflow where the person remains the authority.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="architecture-study" aria-labelledby="study-title">
  <div class="page-shell study-layout">
    <div class="study-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Documented example / RepoPact Core</p>
      <h2 id="study-title">One semantic authority. Several useful views.</h2>
      <p>RepoPact Core places governed records in the repository and uses its canonical Rust engine to interpret, validate, and prepare supported typed operations. The CLI and Workbench are clients. Dashboards, indexes, and interface screens are derived views.</p>
      <p>The interface helps a person navigate the system while the checked-in records remain the source of authority.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/ForgeWireLabs/repopact-core/blob/614689b127cf52f801877cc48440f7e45c3709eb/README.md">Read the Core architecture and authority documentation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
    <figure class="architecture-figure architecture-figure--large">
      <img src="{{ site.basePath }}/assets/repopact-architecture.svg" alt="RepoPact Core architecture diagram showing repository records as authoritative, a Rust semantic engine and CLI or Workbench clients, derived dashboard and graph views, optional integrations, and evidence records." width="1200" height="720" loading="lazy">
      <figcaption>RepoPact Core architecture from its public documentation. The diagram describes Core; other portfolio projects have separate architectures.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

